# Power: let the A core sleep with the screen on, and poll the wheel less often.
#
# Main loop (mod00 0x0306a16c): stock reaches WFI (FUN_03059a04 at 0x0306a184)
# only when msg 0x18 is set, i.e. after the screen-off timeout. With the screen
# on (menus, Now Playing, pause) the A core spins at 100 %. Sleep on every pass
# instead unless msg 0x1f (screen-timeout inhibit: USB mod10, mod13/17/30) is
# set; the recording check (FUN_030599b8) stays. Every IRQ still ends the WFI.
0:0306a16c:1f20                 # movs r0,#0x1f   (was #0x18)
0:0306a174:08d0                 # beq skip-WFI    (was bne: skip unless 0x18)

# Scroll wheel: timer 0 (IRQ 0x23, FUN_03065fd4 -> FUN_03063100) samples the
# quadrature pins GPIO2.14/2.15 every 400 us = 2500 wakeups/s. A fast spin is
# ~300 state changes/s, so 1 ms still samples each state ~3 times.
# mov.w r2,#400 -> #1000 (period in us, FUN_03053a4e) at every timer-0 setup.
0:0306b2cc:4ff47a72             # kernel init
1:03079f9c:4ff47a72             # boot init
9:0307c4a8:4ff47a72
33:03082b7c:4ff47a72            # music service
